@flexiarg task-selection/what-others-wait-on-first
@title What Others Wait On, First
@keywords leverage, unblocking, predecessor, cone, ordering
@audience agents and the War Machine selecting the next task
@tone design
@style pattern
@status draft 2026-10-28 (claude-11, witnesses K4, K5)
@role order
@guard needs: ready candidates (after only-what-can-start-now) and, for each, the items its completion would make ready (Giraffe one-step unblocks).
@effect orders ready candidates by how many items their completion makes ready at once.
@predicts after the task closes, the number of ready items rises by the predicted count.
@references [task-selection/only-what-can-start-now task-selection/prepare-the-ground task-selection/take-the-cheap-win]
! conclusion: Among items that can start now, do first the one that the most other items are waiting on.

  + context: Several items are ready; their completions free different amounts of other work.

  + IF:
    One ready item is a predecessor of several others.

  + HOWEVER:
    Plans are often written in another order (the order pieces were thought of), and the item many others need may be harder or less visible than a cheap uncoupled one.

  + THEN:
    Order the ready items by one-step unblocking and reorder plans when a predecessor is found. When the cheap visible option is chosen instead, record that the high-leverage one was deferred and why.

  + BECAUSE:
    The pieces many others wait on, done first, let several chains close; skipped, those chains grow without closing.

  + evidence:
    - futon3c/holes/missions/M-giraffe.md:289-293 (Joe 2026-10-27): "prefer tasks that can be done now and tasks that unblock others ... they closed 72 problems in two weeks, while the same seats working from a dependency map without them let two chains grow for weeks without closing anything."
    - futon4/holes/missions/M-interest-network-coupling.md:544-549: step (b) gated four items, so "the reshuffle was: step (b) FIRST".
    - futon4/holes/missions/M-writing-ethics.md:262-264: "Claim-ledger: highest leverage ... Unblocks ~5–8 items. Low cost, high yield."

  + counter-evidence: futon3/holes/missions/M-pattern-ingest.md:312-317 chose the cheapest uncoupled option and recorded "(iii) is the highest-leverage cross-mission move but should wait."

  + data: Giraffe unblocks, futon3c/src/futon3c/giraffe/pass.clj:270-285; order row (ready, then unblocks, then cone, then source order) :300-322.
